From 4b02dddaaca5421eeca388b902678d36621e8c4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 02:59:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban pacing: a lapsed pace offer refuses the
 launch instead of starting on the held route

Review t_4a9207abeea5da73 (PR #3301 @419ec4f9): the governor released a paced
card only because its offer would move it to a pool with room, but take()
treated an expired or mismatched offer like no offer, so a claim whose workspace
preparation outlived the 120 s TTL started on the held provider.

- take() now distinguishes "no offer" (ordinary admission, None) from an offer
  that expired or was judged on another route (OfferLost). A resolver failure on
  a card holding an offer raises OfferLost too (lose()).
- OfferLost is refused before spawn as a no-penalty admission deferral
  (admission_refusal infrastructure): the card is requeued and the next tick
  re-runs the governor, never launching the held route.
- hold() withdraws the card's previous offer before each fresh judgment, so an
  offer left by a tick whose claim never ran cannot steer a later admission.
- TTL raised to 600 s so ordinary slow workspace preparation does not lapse it.

Tests: dispatch-level regressions through the real dispatch_once for an offer
expiring during launch (refused, requeued with zero failures, then started on
Grok after the cooldown), a route mismatch, an unresolvable route, and a stale
earlier-tick offer; unit take()/withdraw() contracts. 8 fail before, pass after.
